{"case_id":"G36","elapsed_s":0.000315,"value":{"candidates":[],"candidates_truncated":false,"canonical_status":"canonical","citations":[],"contract_version":"2","descriptions":[{"evidence_id":"danbooru-complete-a26a3829dd42:a26a3829dd42155848392c0636daebd6ca01acf540d3509fec2ac3219f8596c5:line:19077","original":"[b]Mahou Shoujo Madoka Magica[/b], also known as [b]Puella Magi Madoka Magica[/b], is a multimedia franchise created by Magica Quartet, focusing on a world in which young girls can make a contract with [[Kyubey]] to become [[Magical Girl]]s - in return, becoming duty-bound to fight [[Witch (madoka magica)|]]es. Known for its surprisingly dark tone.\r\n\r\nh4. Entries\r\n\r\nh6. Mainline\r\n\r\n* [[Mahou Shoujo Madoka Magica (anime)]] - The original series\r\n** [[Mahou Shoujo Madoka Magica Movie 1 & 2]] - A duology of compilation movies\r\n** [[Mahou Shoujo Madoka Magica Manga]] - The manga adaptation of the series\r\n** [[Mahou Shoujo Madoka Magica Novel]] - The novel adaptation of the series\r\n* Mahou Shoujo Madoka Magica Drama CDs - A series of audio dramas featuring the main cast in alternate scenarios \r\n** Mahou Shoujo Madoka Magica: The Different Story - A manga that started off as an adaption of the \"Farewell Story\" audio drama\r\n* Mahou Shoujo Madoka Magica: Homura Revenge! - A manga that depicts an alternate take on the final few episodes of the original series\r\n* [[Mahou Shoujo Madoka Magica: Hangyaku no Monogatari]] - A sequel movie that continues the events of the series\r\n** [[Mahou Shoujo Madoka Magica: Majuu Hen]] - The prequel manga to the third movie, taking place between that and the original series\r\n* [[Mahou Shoujo Madoka Magica: Walpurgis no Kaiten]] - The fourth movie in the series\r\n\r\nh6. Games\r\n\r\n* [[Mahou Shoujo Madoka Magica Mobage]]\r\n* [[Mahou Shoujo Madoka Magica Portable]] - A [[PlayStation Portable]] video game based on the series\r\n* [[Mahou Shoujo Madoka Magica Plus]]\r\n* [[Mahou Shoujo Madoka Magica Online]]\r\n\r\nh6. Concepts\r\n\r\n* [[Mahou Shoujo Madoka Magica: Concept Movie]] - The initial concept for the fourth movie, which was later reworked into Walpurgis no Kaiten\r\n\r\nh6. Spin-offs\r\n\r\n* [[Mahou Shoujo Kazumi Magica]]\r\n* [[Mahou Shoujo Oriko Magica]]\r\n* [[Mahou Shoujo Tart Magica]]\r\n* [[Mahou Shoujo Suzune Magica]]\r\n* [[Tomoe Mami no Heibon na Nichijou]]\r\n* [[Magia Record: Mahou Shoujo Madoka Magica Gaiden]] - A mobile game spin-off which expanded with its own anime and even a stage musical starring [[Hinatazuka46]]\r\n* [[Null Mahou Shoujo]]\r\n* [[Mahou Shoujo Madoka Magica Magia Exedra]] \r\n\r\nh6. Other\r\n\r\n* [[Grief Syndrome]] - Doujin game\r\n* Manga Time Kirara Magica (pool #19682) - A magazine revolving around the series that was a spin-off of the magazine [[Manga Time Kirara]]\r\n\r\nh4. Related tags\r\n\r\nh6. Memes\r\n\r\n* [[Homu]] \r\n* [[I just don't get it (madoka_magica)|]]\r\n* [[I'm such a fool]] \r\n* [[It sucks to be alone]]\r\n* [[Keep this a secret from everyone in class]]\r\n* [[Make a contract]] \r\n* [[Mami mogu mogu]]\r\n* [[minna shinu shika nai ja nai!]] \r\n* [[Morning Rescue]] \r\n* [[Not afraid anymore]] \r\n* [[Pulque]] \r\n* [[Tengaron Gentleman]]\r\n* [[Too bad! It was just me! (meme)|]] \r\n* [[Want some? (Madoka Magica)]]\r\n* [[Holy Quintet]]\r\n\r\nh6. Theme songs \r\n\r\n* [[Connect (Madoka Magica)|]] - Opening theme of the original series\r\n* [[Magia (Madoka Magica)|]] - Closing theme of the original series \r\n* [[Luminous (Madoka Magica)|]] - Opening theme of movies 1 and 2\r\n* [[Colorful (Madoka Magica)|]] - Opening theme of Hangyaku no Monogatari \r\n* [[Kimi no Gin no Niwa (madoka magica)|]] - Closing theme of Hangyaku no Monogatari \r\n* [[Kanata (FictionJunction)|]] - Main theme of Walpurgis no Kaiten\r\n\r\nh4. See also\r\n\r\n* [[List of Mahou Shoujo Madoka Magica characters]]\r\n\r\nh4. External Links \r\n\r\n* \"Puella Magi Wiki (EN)\":https://wiki.puella-magi.net/Main_Page\r\n* \"Puella Magi Wiki (JP)\":https://w.atwiki.jp/madoka-magica\r\n* \"Wikipedia: Puella Magi Madoka Magica\":https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Puella_Magi_Madoka_Magica","response_truncated":false,"search_text_truncated":false,"source_id":"danbooru-complete-a26a3829dd42","status":"source_backed","title":"mahou_shoujo_madoka_magica"}],"evidence_chain":[{"evidence_id":"native:592923","fetched_at_utc":"2026-09-30T06:43:34.899059+00:00","raw_path":"reports/P3/raw/4ccce02e466f4f14ee4a5252b48b72c33b53db57c6b470fe7307e40a3668a7b8.raw","raw_sha256":"4ccce02e466f4f14ee4a5252b48b72c33b53db57c6b470fe7307e40a3668a7b8","role":"native_identity","source_id":"danbooru-native-scoped-4ccce02e466f","tag_id":592923},{"alias_id":6863,"antecedent_name":"puella_magi_madoka_magica","consequent_name":"mahou_shoujo_madoka_magica","evidence_id":"official_alias:6863","fetched_at_utc":"2026-09-30T07:07:37.788051+00:00","raw_path":"reports/P3/raw/a081193ffbb4a312ab53aaa1b2bc17bc9d0fa944443510c4351a69983eae3b28.raw","raw_sha256":"a081193ffbb4a312ab53aaa1b2bc17bc9d0fa944443510c4351a69983eae3b28","role":"official_alias_step","source_id":"danbooru-native-scoped-4ccce02e466f","upstream_status":"active"},{"active_alias_ids":[6863],"coverage":"scoped_complete","evidence_id":"scope:puella_magi_madoka_magica","fetched_at_utc":"2026-09-30T07:07:37.788051+00:00","name":"puella_magi_madoka_magica","raw_path":"reports/P3/raw/a081193ffbb4a312ab53aaa1b2bc17bc9d0fa944443510c4351a69983eae3b28.raw","raw_sha256":"a081193ffbb4a312ab53aaa1b2bc17bc9d0fa944443510c4351a69983eae3b28","role":"canonical_scope","source_id":"danbooru-native-scoped-4ccce02e466f"},{"active_alias_ids":[],"coverage":"scoped_complete","evidence_id":"scope:mahou_shoujo_madoka_magica","fetched_at_utc":"2026-09-30T06:44:15.981046+00:00","name":"mahou_shoujo_madoka_magica","raw_path":"reports/P3/raw/4f53cda18c2baa0c0354bb5f9a3ecbe5ed12ab4d8e11ba873c2f11161202b945.raw","raw_sha256":"4f53cda18c2baa0c0354bb5f9a3ecbe5ed12ab4d8e11ba873c2f11161202b945","role":"canoni